content.thinking:
I've confirmed the bug. The issue is in the `combine` function in `lib/utils.js`. When `a` is an overflow object and `b` is an array, the function adds the entire array as a single element instead of spreading the values.

Looking at the code:

```javascript
var combine = function combine(a, b, arrayLimit, plainObjects, throwOnLimitExceeded) {
    // If 'a' is already an overflow object, add to it
    if (isOverflow(a)) {
        if (throwOnLimitExceeded) {
            throw new RangeError('Array limit exceeded. Only ' + arrayLimit + ' element' + (arrayLimit === 1 ? '' : 's') + ' allowed in an array.');
        }
        var newIndex = getMaxIndex(a) + 1;
        a[newIndex] = b;   // <-- BUG: When b is an array, it adds the whole array as a single element
        setMaxIndex(a, newIndex);
        return a;
    }
    // ...
};
```

The fix is to check if `b` is an array and, if so, iterate through it and add each element individually. Let me implement this fix.

